window.products.push({"id":126304,"name":"WPW10006355 Washer Actuator Part W10006355 Shift Whirlpool Maytag AP6014711 PS11747977 WTW5640XW3 NTW4600YQ1 MVWC360AW0 MVWC400XW4 MVWX600BW0 MVWC350A","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":22.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71z+J1s-yYS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Maytag Shift Actuator Wpw10006355 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP6014711, W10006355, PS11747977, WPW10006355VP. Actuator W10006355 is compatible with Whirlpool, Maytag, Kenmore, Amana, Admiral, Crosley, Roper appliances. Shift Actuator Wpw10006355 includes a transmission speed / position optical sensor. A synchronous motor is present in the system which moves the splutch cam ring and keeps track of the splutch's position. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Whirlpool W10006355 Actuator? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Maytag Washer Actuator Wpw10006355 will help if your appliance pumps but does not spin; does not agitate / start, or spins slowly. Replacing the Wpw10006355 Shift Actuator is a straightforward process that can be done with basic tools. 💡 Actuator WPW10006355 is made of durable materials that are designed to withstand the stress and wear and tear of regular use. The actuator is a small, rectangular-shaped device that is mounted on the bottom of the washer's gearcase. It works in conjunction with the washer's motor and cam bar to shift the transmission from agitation to spin mode and vice versa. Wpw10006355 Actuator meets or exceed all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How does an actuator get damaged? An actuator can get damaged due to various reasons, including wear and tear from regular use, electrical surges or power fluctuations, physical damage from mishandling or accidents, or exposure to harsh environmental conditions such as extreme temperatures or dust. Additionally, using the washer beyond its recommended capacity or operating it improperly can also lead to actuator damage. Timely diagnosis and replacement of the faulty part is crucial. 💡 How do you test a washer shift actuator? To test a Wpw10006355 Actuator, you can start by unplugging the washer and accessing the actuator. Then, using a multimeter, you can check for continuity in the actuator's motor and switch circuits. If either circuit is open, the actuator is likely defective and needs to be replaced. You can also manually test the Whirlpool Shift Actuator Wpw10006355 by applying power to it and observing whether it moves smoothly between the agitate and spin positions.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71z+J1s-yYS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B089T3R7RH","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-126304","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B089T3R7RH","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B089T3R7RH","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
